<!-- SUMMARY -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-header"><h2>Profile</h2></div>
  <p class="summary">
    Independent researcher and security consultant operating across <strong>distributed systems, post-quantum cryptography, machine learning, and full-stack engineering</strong>.
 Sole architect of GhostWire — a P2P encrypted mesh platform built in 
Rust over one year, combining ML-KEM-768, Double Ratchet, Sphinx onion 
routing, and a 4-layer AI routing system. Author of four published Rust 
crates. GCD4F 2026 competitor across five Kenyan universities. 
Production deployments across restaurant tech, threat intelligence, 
voice AI, and East African fintech infrastructure. Available for <strong>security consulting, architecture advisory, and systems research engagements</strong>. Treats security as a research discipline — not a checklist.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- CORE EXPERIENCE -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-header"><h2>Research &amp; Consulting Experience</h2></div>

  <div class="entry">
    <div class="entry-header">
      <div>
        <div class="entry-title">Sole Architect — GhostWire</div>
        <div class="entry-org">Self-Directed · Open Source · AGPL-3.0 · v0.2.0</div>
      </div>
      <div class="entry-date">2024 – Present</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metrics-row">
      <div class="metric"><span class="num">571K</span><span class="label">Lines Rust</span></div>
      <div class="metric"><span class="num">304</span><span class="label">Source Files</span></div>
      <div class="metric"><span class="num">178</span><span class="label">Tests</span></div>
      <div class="metric"><span class="num">4</span><span class="label">Published Crates</span></div>
      <div class="metric"><span class="num">5</span><span class="label">Universities · GCD4F</span></div>
    </div>
    <ul class="entry-desc">
      <li>Designed and built a post-quantum P2P mesh communication 
platform in Rust — sole architect across cryptographic, network, AI 
routing, and application layers.</li>
      <li>Crypto stack: ML-KEM-768 hybrid KEM, XChaCha20-Poly1305, 
Double Ratchet via vodozemac (Matrix Olm/Megolm), Ed25519 identity, 
Sphinx onion routing, Shamir's Secret Sharing, Argon2, Hybrid Logical 
Clocks.</li>
      <li>Network layer: libp2p 0.56 (TCP, BLE, DTN), SKademlia 
Sybil-resistant DHT, GossipSub, Ghost Channels anonymous broadcast, 
stealth TCP transport with timing randomisation and connection 
obfuscation.</li>
      <li>AI routing: 4-model ensemble — LightGBM/ONNX (&lt;1ms) → Gemma
 4 Ollama (50–200ms) → GNN PyTorch Geo → PRoPHET fallback — trained on 
real 63-node Guifi.net data.</li>
      <li>Live A↔B encrypted messaging test conducted between Omen (Arch Linux) and Stratos (Bedrock Linux). TUI built with ratatui.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag">Rust</span><span class="tag">ML-KEM-768</span><span class="tag">libp2p</span>
      <span class="tag">Vodozemac</span><span class="tag">Sphinx Routing</span><span class="tag">PyTorch</span>
      <span class="tag">ONNX</span><span class="tag">Tokio</span><span class="tag">Ratatui</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="entry">
    <div class="entry-header">
      <div>
        <div class="entry-title">Head of Security</div>
        <div class="entry-org">RVC (Rift Valley Cybersecurity) · Nairobi · Virtual Startup</div>
      </div>
      <div class="entry-date">2024 – Present</div>
    </div>
    <ul class="entry-desc">
      <li>Own security architecture, threat modelling, incident response policy, and security tooling for the organisation.</li>
      <li>Designed and deployed Sentry 2.0 — a production-grade Rust 
HIDS/DLP engine with 3-component architecture: file integrity monitoring
 (15+ DLP patterns), transparent proxy (port 7070), and iptables-based 
egress DPI gate. Auto-restarts via systemd user units. Covers AWS, 
GitHub, Stripe, Anthropic, Slack, Tailscale, M-Pesa, and Safaricom 
credential patterns.</li>
      <li>Built RVC company website (v4) — 6-page static site deployed on Vercel.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag">Rust</span><span class="tag">HIDS</span><span class="tag">DLP</span>
      <span class="tag">iptables</span><span class="tag">systemd</span><span class="tag">Arch Linux</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="entry">
    <div class="entry-header">
      <div>
        <div class="entry-title">Freelance Full-Stack Engineer</div>
        <div class="entry-org">Passua Bites · Nairobi Restaurant · Production</div>
      </div>
      <div class="entry-date">2025 – Present</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metrics-row">
      <div class="metric"><span class="num">140+</span><span class="label">TS/TSX Files</span></div>
      <div class="metric"><span class="num">4,058</span><span class="label">Lines Server</span></div>
      <div class="metric"><span class="num">40+</span><span class="label">Menu Items</span></div>
      <div class="metric"><span class="num">6</span><span class="label">API Routers</span></div>
    </div>
    <ul class="entry-desc">
      <li>Architected and built a full-stack restaurant web app — online
 ordering, menu management, customer reviews, admin dashboard with 
analytics, and payment processing.</li>
      <li>Stack: React 19, TypeScript, tRPC v11, Express, Drizzle ORM, 
Neon PostgreSQL (serverless), shadcn/ui (50+ Radix components), TanStack
 React Query, AWS S3, Google Maps API, Google OAuth.</li>
      <li>Built 6 API router modules: menu, orders, payments, reviews, 
admin, analytics. 4 Drizzle migrations. Deployed on Vercel with 
Cloudflare DNS. M-Pesa Daraja integration in progress.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag">React 19</span><span class="tag">tRPC v11</span><span class="tag">Drizzle ORM</span>
      <span class="tag">Neon PostgreSQL</span><span class="tag">Vercel</span><span class="tag">M-Pesa</span>
    </div>
